vkd3d-proton: MADEIRA_VKD3D_ATOMIC64=1 reports the 64-bit atomic caps

Madeira, 2026-11-27. LGPL-2.1-or-later like vkd3d-proton.

RE Engine (PRAGMATA) checks D3D12_OPTIONS11.AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported
at startup and quits with "Unsupported graphics card ... Apple A20 Pro GPU is not supported
AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported" when it is FALSE. vkd3d-proton sets it from
shaderBufferInt64Atomics and minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment <= 16, which KosmicKrisp on
Apple GPUs does not meet. With MADEIRA_VKD3D_ATOMIC64=1 that cap and options9's
AtomicInt64OnTypedResourceSupported / AtomicInt64OnGroupSharedSupported read TRUE, with an
INFO line giving the driver's own values. Off by default. Madeira's own D3D12 already
answers TRUE here. A shader that actually uses a 64-bit atomic then passes vkd3d's own
check and may fail at pipeline creation instead.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/device.c b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
index bf8aabf..bff8bc4 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -8152,6 +8152,27 @@ static void d3d12_device_caps_init_feature_options11(struct d3d12_device *device
     options11->AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported =
             device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_features.shaderBufferInt64Atomics &&
             device->device_info.properties2.properties.limits.minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment <= 16;
+
+    /* Madeira (MADEIRA_VKD3D_ATOMIC64=1): report the three 64-bit atomic caps even
+     * when the driver lacks them. RE Engine (PRAGMATA) refuses to start without
+     * AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported ("Unsupported graphics card"),
+     * and KosmicKrisp on Apple GPUs does not offer 64-bit buffer atomics. Runs
+     * after options9 is filled in. A shader that really uses a 64-bit atomic then
+     * passes vkd3d's own check and may fail at pipeline creation instead. */
+    {
+        char env[8];
+        if (vkd3d_get_env_var("MADEIRA_VKD3D_ATOMIC64", env, sizeof(env)) && env[0] == '1')
+        {
+            D3D12_FEATURE_DATA_D3D12_OPTIONS9 *options9 = &device->d3d12_caps.options9;
+            INFO("MADEIRA_VKD3D_ATOMIC64: forcing 64-bit atomic caps (driver: heap %u, typed %u, groupshared %u).\n",
+                    options11->AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported,
+                    options9->AtomicInt64OnTypedResourceSupported,
+                    options9->AtomicInt64OnGroupSharedSupported);
+            options11->AtomicInt64OnDescriptorHeapResourceSupported = TRUE;
+            options9->AtomicInt64OnTypedResourceSupported = TRUE;
+            options9->AtomicInt64OnGroupSharedSupported = TRUE;
+        }
+    }
 }
 
 static void d3d12_device_caps_init_feature_options12(struct d3d12_device *device)
